  "id": "COMPOUND:29473 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol and HepG2, a human liver cancer cell line, through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is implicated in targeting SK-VLB and VMRC-LCP, which are both targets of 2-Ethyl-1,3-dioxolane and Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, respectively. These compounds are known to interact with HepG2 cells, indicating a possible mechanism of action involving cellular targets that ultimately affect the cancer cell. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct effect of (Z)-7-Hydroxynuciferol on HepG2 cells.",
